# ABP Data Transfer Objects (DTOs)

## DTO Location
Define DTOs in `*.Application.Contracts` project.

## DTO Base Classes
```csharp
// For entities with Id
public class BookDto : EntityDto<Guid>
{
    public string Name { get; set; }
}

// For audited entities
public class BookDto : AuditedEntityDto<Guid>
{
    public string Name { get; set; }
}

// For extensible entities
public class BookDto : ExtensibleEntityDto<Guid>
{
    public string Name { get; set; }
}
```

## Input DTOs
```csharp
public class CreateBookDto
{
    [Required]
    [StringLength(BookConsts.MaxNameLength)]
    public string Name { get; set; }

    [Range(0, 999.99)]
    public decimal Price { get; set; }
}

public class UpdateBookDto
{
    // ID should NOT be here - passed separately
    [Required]
    [StringLength(BookConsts.MaxNameLength)]
    public string Name { get; set; }
}

public class GetBookListDto : PagedAndSortedResultRequestDto
{
    public string Filter { get; set; }
    public BookType? Type { get; set; }
}
```

## Best Practices
- Don't include unused properties in input DTOs
- Don't share input DTOs between methods
- Don't use inheritance between input DTOs
- Use constants from Domain.Shared for validation (e.g., `BookConsts.MaxNameLength`)
- Prefer Basic DTO and Detailed DTO strategy for output
- Include reference details as nested basic DTOs
- Don't use `[Serializable]` attribute
- No logic in DTOs (except `IValidatableObject` when necessary)
